Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(cookies): Read cookie_perms from the request cookies

Frappe v16 removed frappe.oauth.get_cookie_dict_from_headers, so
press.api.cookies fails to import on v16. The request already exposes
parsed cookies. Werkzeug returns the value as a string, so the .value
access goes. Kept unquote as before, so a value that a browser sends
percent-encoded still parses.
---
 press/api/cookies.py | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/press/api/cookies.py b/press/api/cookies.py
index 3f2b4f4..c281037 100644
--- a/press/api/cookies.py
+++ b/press/api/cookies.py
@@ -4,7 +4,6 @@ from urllib.parse import unquote
 
 import frappe
 from frappe.auth import CookieManager
-from frappe.oauth import get_cookie_dict_from_headers
 
 
 @frappe.whitelist(allow_guest=True)
@@ -15,10 +14,10 @@ def update_preferences(preferences):
 		frappe.local.cookie_manager = CookieManager()
 
 	cookie_manager = frappe.local.cookie_manager
-	cookie_perms = get_cookie_dict_from_headers(frappe.local.request).get("cookie_perms")
+	cookie_perms = frappe.local.request.cookies.get("cookie_perms")
 
 	if cookie_perms:
-		cookie_perms = json.loads(unquote(cookie_perms.value))
+		cookie_perms = json.loads(unquote(cookie_perms))
 
 		# If was disabled before, now enabled or vice-versa
 		if cookie_perms.get("analytics") != preferences_dict.get("analytics"):
